{title: A Hymn of Glory Let Us Sing}
{artist: The Venerable Bede · tr. Benjamin Webb & Elizabeth Rundle Charles}
{key: D}
{time: 6/4}
{tempo: 160}

Verse 1
A hymn of glory let us sing! New hymns throughout the world shall ring:
Alleluia! Alleluia! Christ by a way none ever trod,
Ascends unto the throne of God. Alleluia!

Verse 2
The angels say to the elev'n, "Why stand ye gazing into heav'n?"
Alleluia! Alleluia! This is the Savior This is He!
Jesus has triumphed gloriously. Alleluia!

Verse 3
Again shall ye behold Him so As ye today have seen Him go;
Alleluia! Alleluia! Calm soaring through the radiant sky,
Mounting its dazzling summits high. Alleluia!

Verse 4
May our affections there do tend, And with unwearied hearts ascend,
Alleluia! Alleluia! Toward Thy kingdom's throne where Thou
As in our faith are seated now. Alleluia!

Verse 5
Be Thou our present joy O Lord! Who will be ever our reward,
Alleluia! Alleluia! And, as the countless ages flee,
May all our glory be in Thee! Alleluia!

Chorus
Alleluia! Alleluia! Alleluia! Alleluia!
